# Line endings are normalised here, not left to each machine's git config.
#
# Without this, files bounced between CRLF and LF depending on which tool
# wrote them last, and a sixteen-line edit could land as a 372-line diff of
# pure line-ending churn -- noise that hides real changes in review and
# conflicts between concurrent sessions.
#
# text=auto: git decides text vs binary by content, stores text as LF.
# eol=lf: text files are checked out as LF on every platform, including
# Windows, so a file written by one tool matches what git has.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats git must never inspect or convert. text=auto's heuristic
# usually gets these right, but a .docx or .pdf silently rewritten as text
# is corrupted beyond repair, so they are declared rather than guessed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
